    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the project's only test class is `AcceptanceTest`; the other files are its base/support classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment on owner creation, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `customerCode` field (`customer_code` column) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added `assignCustomerCode(owner)` in `addOwner`, called after mapping and before saving. It builds the code from the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` and a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to `findAllOwners().size() + 1` (the current owner count plus one), via `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", prefix, sequence)`.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Ignored `customerCode` on the `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` create mapping (it's assigned in the controller); the `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` mapping picks it up automatically by name so it's returned on `GET`.\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` response schema so it's exposed in the generated DTO/API.\n\n5. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added the `customer_code` column to `hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, and `postgres` `schema.sql` (hsqldb is what the tests use; `ddl-auto=none` there so the DDL column is required).\n\n**Behavior verified by the test:** two owners `smithers` then `jones` get `SMI-XXXX` and `JON-YYYY` where `YYYY = XXXX + 1`, because the count is read before saving each owner. Assigning the code before `saveOwner` means the first new owner gets `count+1` and the next gets `count+2`, giving the consecutive sequence.",
